@startuml
title SQ-01 - Find and compare laptop offers (UC1, supplementary sequence)
autonumber "<b>00"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam dpi 140
skinparam maxMessageSize 170
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #555555
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFF4F4
  ParticipantBorderColor #B52330
  ActorBackgroundColor #EEEEEE
  ActorBorderColor #202025
  GroupBorderColor #B52330
}
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FAF5F5
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B52330

actor Shopper
participant "Shopper\nClient" as UI
participant "Shopping\nAPI" as API
participant "Catalog\nQuery" as CAT
participant "Price\nEvidence" as EV
participant "Advice\nEngine" as ADV
database "Data\nStore" as DB

Shopper -> UI : enter search, filters and sorting; optionally select up to three laptops
UI -> API : findProducts(criteria, selected ids)
activate API
API -> API : validate the criteria (text, price bounds, sort order)\nand normalise the query
API -> CAT : findProducts(criteria)
activate CAT
CAT -> DB : readMatchingVariantsAndLatestOffers(criteria)
DB --> CAT : laptops with offers (retailer, price, currency, observedAt)
CAT -> CAT : group exact variants; keep comparable currency only
alt matching laptops exist
  CAT -> CAT : sort as requested; flag offers older than the freshness limit
  CAT --> API : ranked laptops and offers
  opt two or three laptops are selected
    loop each selected laptop
      API -> EV : getEvidence(productId)
      EV --> API : best offer, reference, delta, sufficiency
      API -> ADV : advise(productId, evidence)
      ADV --> API : advice and forecast status
    end
    API -> API : build the side-by-side table:\nbest offer, delta, forecast status, advice
  end
else no matching laptop
  CAT --> API : empty result
  API -> API : add suggested filter changes (widen the price range, drop a brand)
end
deactivate CAT
API --> UI : results, comparison table, sources and observation times
deactivate API
UI --> Shopper : show offers with provenance and freshness

note over API, DB
  Only exact variants and prices in a comparable currency are compared. UC1 is read-only and forces no new
  component, so it is a supplementary sequence and not an architecturally significant use case.
end note
@enduml
